SUMMARY:🌳☀️ HIGH PARK SUNDAY WALK & PICNIC ☀️🌳
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🌳
 ☀️ HIGH PARK SUNDAY WALK & PICNIC ☀️🌳\n\n**Toronto's Biggest Pa
 rk\, Hidden Trails\, The Zoo & A Relaxing Sunday Afternoon**\n\nThere are 
 few better ways to spend a Sunday than wandering through High Park with go
 od people\, great conversation\, and no real rush to be anywhere.\n\nJoin 
 us for a relaxed afternoon exploring Toronto's largest and most beloved pa
 rk. High Park has a little bit of everything—peaceful forest trails\, be
 autiful gardens\, Grenadier Pond\, wildlife\, open green spaces\, and even
  its own free zoo. It's one of those places where you can forget you're in
  Canada's largest city.\n\nThis isn't about racing from one landmark to an
 other.\nIt's about slowing down\, getting outside\, meeting new people\, a
 nd enjoying a few hours together in one of Toronto's best parks.\n\n📲 *
 *Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com
 /DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll
  spend approximately **3 hours** exploring many of High Park's most beauti
 ful areas at a relaxed social pace.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n🌳 Wander t
 hrough shaded forest trails\n🦆 Visit beautiful Grenadier Pond\n🦙 Sto
 p by the famous High Park Zoo to visit the animals\n🌼 Explore some of t
 he park's quieter hidden corners\n🧺 Take a relaxing **30-minute picnic 
 break**\, giving everyone a chance to sit\, eat\, chat\, and get to know o
 ne another\n\n😊 Enjoy one of Toronto's best Sunday afternoons together\
 n\nThis route avoids the large staircase found on some of our other High P
 ark walks\, making it a little more relaxed. There are still a few gentle 
 hills throughout the park\, but nothing overly challenging for most walker
 s.\nThe goal isn't simply to walk through High Park.\nThe goal is to creat
 e enough time together that conversations can happen naturally and new fri
 endships have a chance to begin.\n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather & Expectation
 s\n\nThis walk takes place rain or shine.\nPlease dress appropriately for 
 the weather and wear comfortable walking shoes.\nWe'll keep a relaxed\, st
 eady pace with plenty of opportunities to enjoy the scenery and chat along
  the way.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Hi
 gh Park Sign (west side of Bloor Street & High Park Avenue)\n🫎 I'll be 
 wearing my **Moose Hat**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **11:00 AM**\nI will only w
 ait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\nWe'll leave pr
 omptly so everyone can enjoy the full walk together.\n\n🏁 **End Point:*
 * Back at High Park Subway Station\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$5
  cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto
 :mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows
  us to continue organizing events like this. Thank you for supporting comm
 unity! 💖\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortabl
 e walking shoes\n🧺 Lunch or snacks for our picnic break\n🥪 Something
  small to share with the group if you'd like\n🧴 Sunscreen\n🕶️ Sung
 lasses\n🐿️ Your Sunday afternoon spirit\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This
  For?\n\nThis group is open to anyone who wants to get outside\, meet new 
 people\, and make friends—whether you're single or not.\nWe also host:\n
 🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Rest
 aurant gatherings\nThere's always something happening.\n\n***\n\n**REMEMBE
 R:** You're always welcome to just show up on the day if you're unsure abo
 ut your schedule.\nAs always\, sometimes plans change and events may need 
 to be cancelled—please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n***
 \n\n👤 **Organizer:** Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email
 \n📧 **[torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandouti
 ngs@hotmail.com)**\n\n**Come for the park.**\n**Stay for the picnic.**\n\n
 **Leave with a few more names in your phone than when you arrived.** 🌳
 🧺✨
