SUMMARY:🌿🚶 Mount Pleasant Cemetery Summer Evening Walk
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n# 🌿
 🚶 Mount Pleasant Cemetery Summer Evening Walk\n\n### Toronto's Most Pea
 ceful Summer Stroll\n\nJoin me for a relaxing **90-minute evening walk** t
 hrough one of Toronto's most beautiful hidden gems — **Mount Pleasant Ce
 metery**. This isn't just a cemetery — it's a living museum\, arboretum\
 , and one of the city's most peaceful green spaces\, with winding paths\, 
 majestic trees\, historic monuments\, and beautiful gardens.\n\nAs the sum
 mer evening light filters through the canopy\, it's easy to forget you're 
 in the middle of Toronto. It's the perfect place to slow down\, enjoy grea
 t conversation\, and connect with friendly people while escaping the noise
  of the city.\n🌿 *Sometimes the best way to end the day is with a walk.
 *\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.w
 hatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n## 💫 Did You Know?\n\nWhen Mount
  Pleasant first opened in **1876**\, it was one of Toronto's favourite Vic
 torian destinations. Families would dress up\, ride the streetcar\, and sp
 end the afternoon strolling the grounds before heading back downtown. Long
  before city parks became popular\, this was one of Toronto's most beloved
  places to walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🕕 Meetup Details\n\n**Meetup Time:** **6:
 00 pm** *(I'll wait 5 minutes.)*\n**Meetup Spot:** Inside the main gates o
 f Mount Pleasant Cemetery at the **Yonge Street entrance** (the large ston
 e archway).\n👀 **Look for me:** I'll be wearing my famous **Moose Hat**
  🦌\n\n**End Spot:** Right back where we started.\n\n***\n\n## 🍽️ D
 inner After\n\nAfter the walk\, anyone who's interested is welcome to join
  us for dinner at Swiss Chalet. It's a great opportunity to continue the c
 onversations and get to know one another.\n\n***\n\n## 💲 Meetup Fee\n\n
 **$5** (cash 💵 or e-transfer 📲 to **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mail
 to:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**)\nYou can send it before or on the day of 
 the walk.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n• Comfortable walking shoes
 \n• Water 💧\n• Sunscreen if needed ☀️\n• Bug spray (optional)
 \n\n***\n\n## ☀️ Weather\n\nThis walk will take place rain or shine\, 
 except in cases of severe weather or thunderstorms.\nPlease check Meetup b
 efore leaving in case of weather updates.\n\n***\n\n## 💬 Final Notes\n\
 n• You can just show up — no need to commit early.\n• Please keep an
  eye on Meetup for any updates.\n\nGet updates\, chat with other walkers\,
  and stay in the loop for future events.\n\n✨ End your day surrounded by
  beautiful gardens\, towering trees\, fascinating history\, and great comp
 any. It's one of Toronto's most peaceful places—and one of the city's be
 st-kept secrets.\n\n**Organizer:** Mathew\n📩 [torontomoviesandoutings@h
 otmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)\n\n**Trade traffic
  for tree-lined paths\, fresh air\, and good conversation. Your evening wi
 ll thank you.** 🌿
